---
description: Direct one immersive-theatre moment through checkpoint-aware safety, dramaturgy, resources, consent and cue control.
args:
  sources: LiveShowSources
  checkpoint: TheatreCheckpoint | null
  event: TheatreEvent
  stageManager: StageManager
returns: TheatreControlProposal
---
Bind previousCheckpoint to the supplied checkpoint, or initialize a complete TheatreCheckpoint with this production identity, unknown state, empty cue receipts and knowledge ledgers, no resource reservations, and no asserted safety all-clear. Bind show as LiveShowState { production: sources.production, checkpoint: previousCheckpoint, scriptEvidence: sources.scriptEvidence, productionEvidence: sources.productionEvidence, safetyRules: sources.safetyRules }. Keep previousCheckpoint immutable. The source record disposition in sources.sourceRecordStatus is neither cue execution nor rehearsal approval. sources.priorRecordIds identify earlier domain records only and must never be copied into executedCueReceiptIds. Preserve sources.reviewAudience as the view recipient; it does not confer stage-manager authority. Bind incident = `inspectShowEvent(show, event)` and preserve its incident statement verbatim. Combine current show production evidence, script evidence, safety rules, event evidence and updates as the evidence set for this review. For checkpoint-only replay before any replacement cue plan exists, bind emptyCueSequence to a CueSequence with empty order, cues, conflicts, pending acknowledgments and execution receipts, and ready false. The replay child still reads observed receipt IDs from the checkpoint; this empty value means only that no new cues are being proposed.

Branch on incident.kind. If it is safety-stop, bind continuity = `holdForSafety(incident, show, event)`. Return a blocked safety-hold proposal immediately using continuity.proposedCheckpoint as resumeState. Preserve prior cue receipt IDs and per-group audience knowledge. Name the authorized safety lead and the exact current all-clear evidence still required. Do not build a scene, route or cue on this branch; language review cannot clear a stop.

For all other events, bind dramaturgy = `modelDramaturgy(show.production, event.sceneIds, evidence)`. If dramaturgy.ready is false, bind replay = `recoverContinuity(show.production, show.checkpoint, incident, dramaturgy, emptyCueSequence, evidence)` to preserve only observed checkpoint receipts and leave unobserved plans untouched. Return blocked with its exact knowledge and reveal-order gaps and replay.proposedCheckpoint as the resumable state.

When the scene graph and knowledge ledger are ready, bind resources = `modelProduction(show.production, dramaturgy, incident, evidence, show.safetyRules)`. Keep its time-window conflicts separate from consent routes. For participant-decline, allow only a documented equivalent quiet path and do not invite again. For cast-absence, require a present qualified performer and signed-off variant. For prop-failure, remove that prop and permit only an approved lighting or sound recovery. For knowledge-divergence, preserve separate audience-group ledgers through route selection. If any safety, access, consent or resource blocker remains, do not select cues; bind replay = `recoverContinuity(show.production, show.checkpoint, incident, dramaturgy, emptyCueSequence, evidence)` and return blocked with exact scene and route blockers and replay.proposedCheckpoint as the resumable state.

Only after resource and consent assessment, bind routes = `selectSceneVariants(incident, dramaturgy, resources, evidence)`. If routes.selected is empty or routes.blockers is nonempty, bind replay = recoverContinuity(show.production, show.checkpoint, incident, dramaturgy, emptyCueSequence, evidence). Return a complete blocked TheatreControlProposal with resumeState: replay.proposedCheckpoint and the actual route blockers; never manufacture a new cue plan to fill the gap.

For an approved route, bind cues = `coordinatePerformance(show.production, routes, resources, evidence)`. Keep every cue proposed or awaiting acknowledgment until its current owner receipt exists. Bind continuity = `recoverContinuity(show.production, show.checkpoint, incident, dramaturgy, cues, evidence)` so executed cue history stays separate from unexecuted plans. Use continuity.proposedCheckpoint as the complete, type-compatible resumeState. Return `TheatreControlProposal` for stageManager.id with only findings relevant to this branch, the exact action boundary, explicit blockers and the new proposed checkpoint. Mark ready-for-review only when script, rehearsal approval, consent, timing, resources and critical role receipts support the selected route and no stop is active. The result is never an approval, dispatch, cue execution or persisted checkpoint.
